figdown 0.1 block
# 0.1 (RULE 1.1a): a POINT is parenthesised, everywhere. Four spellings
# used a bare comma pair — which asserts "a list of two numbers", the wrong
# shape — and each retired form names its migration. Two of the four
# (`path tailport=`/`headport=`) went with their directive
# (`EDGE-GEOMETRY-CONSTRUCTS`); `pin at=` and the `cell` grid address carry the rule now.
# The single-valued forms stay bare: they are not points.
node a "A"
node b "B"
edge a -> b
layout
pin a at=10,20
pin b at=(30,40)
